Job02: Logic You Can Touch

Topic: Sequence, Decision, and Repetition using block-based logic (Scratch).  
Core Concept: Moving from physical/shop floor operational logic (like automated stamping or inspection) to programming logic.  
Key Programming Concepts & Python Mapping
Repetition (Loops):
Block Logic: Run enclosed blocks N times.  
Python Future: for i in range(10):  
Shop Analogy: Stamping 500 blanks using one defined cycle.  
Decision Making (Conditionals):
Block Logic: Test a condition and take one of two paths (accept or reject).  
Python Future: if dia <= limit: ... else:  
Shop Analogy: Go / No-Go Gauge inspection ("If within tolerance \rightarrow accept bin, else \rightarrow reject bin").  
Input / Sensing:
Block Logic: Sensing interaction or key press.  
Python Future: ask() \rightarrow input().  
Variables:
Block Logic: A labeled bin holding a value (counter, score, diameter).  
Python Future: count = 0.
